cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Euler's Pentagonal Number Theorem
  and the Jacobi Triple Product
message: >-
  If you use this formalization in your research, please cite it
  using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jonathan
    family-names: Conrad
  - given-names: Paula
    family-names: Muermann
  - given-names: Maryna
    family-names: Viazovska
repository-code: 'https://github.com/viazovska/PentagonalNumberTheorem'
url: 'https://viazovska.github.io/PentagonalNumberTheorem'
abstract: >-
  Two independent Lean 4 / Mathlib formalizations of Euler's
  pentagonal number theorem. The first follows Franklin's
  sign-reversing involution on partitions into distinct parts and
  yields the coefficient identity for the truncated product. The
  second develops q-Pochhammer symbols, Euler's identities and the
  Cauchy identity to prove the Jacobi Triple Product, both as a
  formal power series identity over an arbitrary commutative ring
  and analytically over the complex numbers for |q| < 1, and
  derives the pentagonal number theorem for the infinite product
  by specialization.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - interactive theorem proving
  - number theory
  - partitions
  - q-series
  - pentagonal number theorem
  - Jacobi triple product
